From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@x>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 16:56:08 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Serein: keep an ordered label selection whose ends scroll out
 of a virtualized list

Upstream pairs the two ends of a label selection by the order labels are shown in a pass and drops the selection when either end is not shown. Labels shown with LabelSelectionState::ordered_label_text_selection carry a SelectionOrder { item, index }: a selection whose ends are both ordered is ranked by that order, kept while an end is not laid out, and cleared when an end is missing between shown labels. Copy with an end out of view assembles bounded retained text (4 MiB charged with allocations, 4,096 labels) and only when every label of the selection was shown with the characters its final ends give it; forget_items marks edited or removed items out of date. A widget that already copied in the pass keeps the clipboard. Adds is_dragging, selection_rect and ordered_ends.
